        "original_id": "fa281e36-5c81-59c3-9e9d-c93070f8dc8b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Jesus Jones, The 77s\n- Music releases: Zeroes and Ones, Perverse\n- Organizations: Fools of the World\n- Places: Bradford-on-Avon, Wiltshire, Sacramento, California\n\nFacts:\n- Jesus Jones are a British alternative rock band from Bradford-on-Avon in Wiltshire that formed in late 1988 and recorded and performed from the late 1980s into the 2000s.\n- The 77s are an American rock band consisting of Michael Roe on vocals and guitar, Mark Harmon on bass, and Bruce Spencer on drums.\n- Zeroes and Ones is the third single from Jesus Jones' 1993 album Perverse.\n- Fools of the World is an independent record label in Sacramento, California that was founded in 1996 by the Christian rock band The 77s.",
